explanation:
I judged this from the body and the docstring and did not search Mathlib for a separate counterpart.

The body uses `mkFunctor`, the universal property of the join. Functors out of C ⋆ D are determined by three pieces of data: a functor on C, a functor on D, and a natural transformation linking them. Here these are:
- `Fₗ ⋙ inclLeft`, i.e. F followed by the inclusion of E into E ⋆ E';
- `Fᵣ ⋙ inclRight`, i.e. G followed by the inclusion of E' into E ⋆ E';
- the natural transformation whose components are the canonical edges `edge (F c) (G d)`.

Naturality holds automatically, because there is at most one morphism from an object of the left part to an object of the right part. This is exactly the standard map F ⋆ G. It works for arbitrary categories and universes, so it is stated at its natural generality.
